\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Sandbox}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}
\tag{environment}

\p{Fix an interactive realization #{\mathsf{Env}_{\mathsf T}} from
\ref{ftip-006T}, a measurable evidence space #{\mathcal E_{\rm box}}, and a cost
dimension #{m\geq1}. A \strong{sandbox} specifies an allowed action set
#{\mathcal A^{\rm box}_{\mathsf T}\subseteq\mathcal A_{\mathsf T}} that is
measurable, a cost bound #{b_{\rm box}\in\mathbb R_+^m}, and, for each
#{x\in\mathcal X_{\mathsf T}} and #{0\leq t<T_{\max}}, an execution kernel}

##{
K_{t}^{\rm box,x}:
\mathcal S_{\mathsf T}\times\mathcal A^{\rm box}_{\mathsf T}
\rightsquigarrow
\mathcal S_{\mathsf T}\times\mathcal O^{\rm obs}_{\mathsf T}
\times\mathcal E_{\rm box}\times\mathbb R_+^m,
}

\p{It also specifies, for each #{x\in\mathcal X_{\mathsf T}}, a reset kernel}

##{
\mathsf{Reset}^{x}_{\rm box}:\{\ast\}\rightsquigarrow
\mathcal S_{\mathsf T}\times\mathcal O^{\rm obs}_{\mathsf T}
\times\mathcal E_{\rm box}\times\mathbb R_+^m.
}

\p{For an allowed action, the state--observation marginal of
#{K_t^{\rm box,x}} is the kernel #{K_t^x} in the task realization; the
state--observation marginal of the reset kernel is #{\rho_0^x}. The remaining
coordinates record reproducible evidence and a realized cost increment. An
admitted stopped trajectory must have componentwise cumulative cost at most
#{b_{\rm box}}.}

\p{The sandbox semantics include permissions, kernel and reset versions,
evidence encoding, and cost accounting. A tool name or API schema alone does
not determine these fields.}
